      "text": "Turtle Island takes its name from the turtles that come ashore to lay their eggs from May to August.\n\nYou can snorkel among the corals just offshore. One Guna family lives on the island. During the day, you can talk with them, walk around the island or relax in a hammock.\n\nDinner is served back on the yacht, with fresh lobster caught that day."
    },
